WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.610
Graham: Look at that silver fox.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.180
So distinguished,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.340
so sophisticated.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.470
Wow!

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.840
But what if I told you

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.879
that this guy was a millennial?

00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:14.910
It's true,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:15.789
just barely.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:16.987
According to Joe,

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:19.878
he started going gray when he was 16.

00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:23.720
By 22, he was pretty much totally gray.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:24.840
Why does that happen?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.683
And why does hair turn
gray in the first place?

00:00:31.893 --> 00:00:35.660
There's something about a silver fox,

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.984
if you can pull it off.

00:00:36.984 --> 00:00:38.630
When I got rid of my gray hair,

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.060
I wanted a natural look.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.910
Graham: But many people
hate the idea of going gray.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.970
There's an entire industry
built around fighting it.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.150
It's like you took off 10 years.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.790
And in just five minutes.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.940
Man: Just For Men.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.190
She'll love the way you look.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.160
Graham: So why does it happen?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.960
The process of hair
changing from darker color

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.260
to white or gray with age
is mainly due to genetics.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.947
It can be inherited from either parent.

00:01:03.947 --> 00:01:05.680
The color of our hair is determined

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.710
by the form of hair pigment that we have.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.730
The pigment is actually
produced along the hair shaft,

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.830
and there are two main
forms of hair pigment.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:13.900
There's eumelanin

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:14.970
and pheomelanin.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.180
Eumelanin is what we see in brunettes

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.320
and darker-haired people,

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.790
and pheomelanin is what we see in blonds

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.623
and redheads.

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:22.980
The cells in our hair bulb

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.970
produce a little bit of hydrogen peroxide,

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.590
which is a metabolic byproduct,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.770
and typically there's an
enzyme called catalase

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.244
that breaks this down to water and oxygen.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.380
But as we age, there's
declining levels of catalase,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.480
and this allows the build-up
of hydrogen peroxide

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.820
in the hair bulb, which damages

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.270
and destroys the melanocytes,

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.995
or the pigment producing
cells, of our hair.

00:01:42.995 --> 00:01:45.250
So I wanted you to take a look

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.875
at my colleague Joe here.

00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:50.451
Joe is technically a millennial.

00:01:50.451 --> 00:01:54.030
He started to go gray when he was 16,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.899
and by 22, it was pretty
much gray all over.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:58.713
What happened to Joe?

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.194
Jennifer: So when individuals
gray early in life

00:02:02.194 --> 00:02:03.700
before the age of 20,

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.903
it's called premature graying,

00:02:04.903 --> 00:02:07.790
and this is due to genes.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.650
And we know there's one gene in particular

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.080
that's been targeted called

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.941
interferon regulatory factor 4,

00:02:12.941 --> 00:02:14.840
which is important in regulating

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.600
and producing melanin in the hair.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.160
Joe was lucky enough to inherit some genes

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.290
that predisposed him to developing
gray hair early in life.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.874
Obviously, Joe has gray hair on his head.

00:02:24.874 --> 00:02:27.130
When you go gray on your head,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.460
does the hair on the
other parts of your body

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.473
go gray as well?

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:32.960
No, no, Joe, Joe!

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.903
We can picture it.

00:02:34.882 --> 00:02:37.340
Jennifer: So you can grow gray
hair anywhere on your body.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.180
Wherever you have hair,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.220
the hair is susceptible
to oxidative damage

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.120
and eventually going gray.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.820
Graham: So the main cause
of going gray is genetics,

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.000
but what role can stress play?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.870
After all, Obama didn't look like this

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.150
when he showed up at the White House.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.200
Jennifer: So it's controversial

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.410
the role that stress has in hair graying.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.100
We know that stress
creates oxidative damage

00:02:59.100 --> 00:02:59.933
in the body,

00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:02.640
and it's been linked to a lot
of premature-aging syndromes.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.300
So it's thought that the stress,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.990
that stress causes oxidative damage,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.800
which may cause damage to the melanocytes

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.955
and may cause us to grow gray earlier.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.660
We know that smokers tend to go gray

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.803
moreso than the general population,

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.268
and again it's felt that
it's probably due to

00:03:20.268 --> 00:03:22.380
the oxidative damage that smoke causes

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.130
and how it affects the
pigment-producing cells in the hair.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.030
I think eating a well-balanced diet,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:27.863
so you make sure

00:03:27.863 --> 00:03:29.560
that you don't develop any
nutritional deficiencies,

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.910
that's another thing that can be done.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.480
And modulating your stress.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.990
That's another thing
you have control over,

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.846
which over time can cause oxidative damage

00:03:35.846 --> 00:03:39.543
and, again, make you prone to
potentially more gray hair.

